.\" Begin generated content:
.TH "kanshi" "1" "2026-02-01"
.PP
.SH "نام (NAME)"
.PP
kanshi \- dynamic output configuration
.PP
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.PP
\fBkanshi\fR [options.\&.\&.\&]
.PP
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Show help message and quit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-c, --config\fR <config>
.RS 4
Specifies a config file.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-l, --listen-fd\fR <fd>
.RS 4
Listen on the specified file descriptor for IPC.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.PP
kanshi is a Wayland daemon that automatically configures outputs.\&
.PP
kanshi is configured with a list of output profiles.\& Each profile contains a set
of outputs.\& A profile will be automatically activated if all specified outputs
are currently connected.\& A profile contains configuration for each output.\&
.PP
If kanshi receives a SIGHUP signal, it will reread its config file.\&
.PP
.SH "پیکربندی (CONFIGURATION)"
.PP
kanshi reads its configuration from \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kanshi/config\fR.\& If unset,
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR defaults to \fB\(ti/.\&config\fR.\&
.PP
An error is raised if no configuration file is found.\&
.PP
For information on the configuration file format, see \fBkanshi\fR(5).\&
.PP
.SH "نویسندگان (AUTHORS)"
.PP
Maintained by Simon Ser <contact@emersion.\&fr>, who is assisted by other
open-source contributors.\& For more information about kanshi development, see
<https://gitlab.\&freedesktop.\&org/emersion/kanshi>.\&
.PP
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.PP
\fBkanshi\fR(5) \fBkanshictl\fR(1)
